{
  "summary": "Moves confirmed spent and conflicted transaction outputs out of the primary wallet TXO set into a separate `m_unusable_txos` map, leaving only spendable or mempool-spent outputs in `m_txos`. In addition, caches output-level metadata (`TxState`, coinbase status, `m_from_me`, timestamp, and transaction version) directly inside `WalletTXO` to avoid dereferencing parent `CWalletTx` objects during iteration. Keeps these containers and cached states synchronized during block connections, disconnections, reorgs, transaction abandonments, and wallet loading.",
  "problem": "Since the wallet began indexing its own transaction outputs in memory (#27286), operations like balance calculation and coin selection iterate over every historical output the wallet ever owned. For wallets with extensive transaction histories, iterating through large numbers of confirmed-spent or conflicted outputs causes CPU overhead and noticeable latency.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'This TXO set is iterated for balance checking and coin selection preparation, which can still be slow for wallets that have had a lot of activity. This PR aims to improve the performance of such wallets by moving UTXOs that are definitely no longer spendable to a different map in the wallet so that far fewer TXOs need to be iterated...'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Touches core wallet state transitions and changes `CWalletTx` serialization by conditionally appending `m_from_me` to disk, accompanied by wallet loading adjustments and backwards compatibility tests.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Adds serialization of the cached `m_from_me` flag to `CWalletTx` on disk, runs transaction reordering immediately after loading transactions, refactors unit test helpers to construct synced wallets via `CWallet::CreateNew`, and adds functional tests for double-spend handling and backward compatibility.",
  "card": "Bitcoin Core's in-memory TXO index traverses every historical output owned by a wallet when checking balances and selecting coins, even outputs spent long ago. This PR moves confirmed spent and conflicted outputs to a separate unusable map so that balance and coin selection routines iterate over a much smaller working set. It also embeds transaction state, version, and confirmation details directly into each WalletTXO to eliminate parent transaction lookups. The change is aimed at improving balance and send performance on wallets with large transaction histories.",
  "needs": [
    "benchmark_numbers"
  ],
